Vendored from kubernetes-sigs/ingress-controller-conformance PR #101 by Tam Mach
(<https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/ingress-controller-conformance/pull/101>).
Cilium maintains this patch in their fork (cilium/ingress-controller-conformance)
because upstream was opened in 2022 but never merged.

The upstream HTTP step does `client.Do(req)` once with no retry budget, so a
single 5xx loses the scenario — even though every Ingress controller has
some non-zero gap between K8s Endpoints update and runtime config push.
PR #101 wraps CaptureRoundTrip in an `awaitConvergence` loop that requires
3 consecutive identical-status-code responses within 30s before accepting
the result. This absorbs short-lived 503s during steady-state convergence
without papering over real bugs (a permanent 5xx still fails the scenario).

Apply with `git apply` from the upstream checkout root. Pinned to commit
d920ed36a0076e169a9a329a850844ab3a695ae8 — bumping that SHA in the Makefile
may require re-resolving this patch.

